1
00:00:48,006 --> 00:00:54,971
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

2
00:00:56,806 --> 00:00:58,641
EPISODE 13

3
00:00:58,725 --> 00:00:59,559
What…

4
00:01:01,102 --> 00:01:02,395
did you just do?

5
00:01:04,814 --> 00:01:06,066
Did you send a bomb

6
00:01:07,859 --> 00:01:09,652
to the residence
through the pneumatic tube?

7
00:01:13,156 --> 00:01:14,616
Answer the question. Did you?

8
00:01:19,162 --> 00:01:21,790
Is that why Hanako…

9
00:01:25,543 --> 00:01:26,419
Answer me.

10
00:01:34,844 --> 00:01:35,845
I'm sorry.

11
00:01:38,348 --> 00:01:39,891
I'm so sorry.

12
00:01:50,401 --> 00:01:51,236
Put the gun down.

13
00:01:57,158 --> 00:01:58,868
She knew nothing about it.

14
00:01:59,661 --> 00:02:01,412
She only made the call as I told her.

15
00:02:06,501 --> 00:02:07,669
I'm sorry

16
00:02:08,503 --> 00:02:09,420
about your sister.

17
00:02:13,299 --> 00:02:14,634
But your father

18
00:02:15,677 --> 00:02:16,886
deserves to die.

19
00:02:24,185 --> 00:02:25,186
Mr. Sato!

20
00:02:26,479 --> 00:02:29,399
Those two <i>Josenjings</i>
are in on it together.

21
00:02:31,151 --> 00:02:32,569
I heard everything.

22
00:02:34,612 --> 00:02:37,740
They were plotting the whole thing.

23
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:41,077
Keum Seo-hee is a spy!

24
00:03:14,527 --> 00:03:15,445
Hanako.

25
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:18,656
Hanako.

26
00:03:20,450 --> 00:03:21,284
Hanako!

27
00:03:21,367 --> 00:03:24,078
Hanako!

28
00:03:25,371 --> 00:03:26,206
Hanako!

29
00:03:26,289 --> 00:03:28,458
- Hanako!
- Hanako!

30
00:03:29,167 --> 00:03:31,252
Hanako, open your eyes.

31
00:03:31,336 --> 00:03:32,253
Hanako!

32
00:03:41,679 --> 00:03:42,680
Hanako.

33
00:03:49,812 --> 00:03:50,813
It's the study!

34
00:03:51,397 --> 00:03:52,899
Protect the inspector general!

35
00:03:53,858 --> 00:03:56,861
Go to His Excellency's residence
and get him to safety.

36
00:03:56,945 --> 00:03:59,322
A bomb might've been sent
from the Government-General.

37
00:03:59,405 --> 00:04:00,406
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

38
00:04:01,699 --> 00:04:02,533
Philip.

39
00:04:03,701 --> 00:04:04,535
Philip!

40
00:04:05,328 --> 00:04:07,163
Philip!

41
00:04:07,705 --> 00:04:09,207
Philip!

42
00:04:09,290 --> 00:04:10,375
Philip.

43
00:04:26,557 --> 00:04:28,476
You can't find Keum Seo-hee?

44
00:04:30,561 --> 00:04:31,479
<i>We have an emergency.</i>

45
00:04:31,562 --> 00:04:32,855
<i>We have an emergency.</i>

46
00:04:32,939 --> 00:04:34,232
<i>A subversive has sent explosives</i>

47
00:04:34,315 --> 00:04:37,485
<i>from the pneumatic tube room</i>
<i>to the inspector general's residence.</i>

48
00:04:37,568 --> 00:04:39,445
<i>We have an emergency.</i>

49
00:04:41,656 --> 00:04:43,950
<i>All guards, report</i>
<i>to the pneumatic tube room immediately!</i>

50
00:04:44,033 --> 00:04:46,619
<i>All personnel, remain at your posts!</i>

51
00:04:46,703 --> 00:04:47,537
<i>I repeat!</i>

52
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:49,664
<i>Report to the pneumatic tube room</i>
<i>immediately!</i>

53
00:04:49,747 --> 00:04:51,416
<i>We have an emergency.</i>

54
00:04:51,499 --> 00:04:53,334
See?

55
00:04:53,418 --> 00:04:55,044
They're the ones--

56
00:05:10,143 --> 00:05:13,146
We'll say Mitarai was a spy
who gave outsiders access

57
00:05:13,771 --> 00:05:14,814
to the Government-General.

58
00:05:17,984 --> 00:05:19,527
Let's get Ms. Lee out of here first.

59
00:05:20,486 --> 00:05:21,863
Seems we're on the same page.

60
00:05:25,074 --> 00:05:26,034
Mr. Sato.

61
00:05:26,784 --> 00:05:27,869
Not now. Later.

62
00:05:29,162 --> 00:05:31,247
Let's get out of here. Then we can talk.

63
00:05:39,714 --> 00:05:40,548
Drop the gun.

64
00:05:41,924 --> 00:05:43,092
Wait, just a second.

65
00:05:43,176 --> 00:05:44,010
Drop the gun!

66
00:05:52,143 --> 00:05:55,188
Use me as a hostage,
and you can get out of here.

67
00:05:55,271 --> 00:05:56,522
Don't give me that bullshit.

68
00:05:57,523 --> 00:06:01,069
You expect me to believe you,
a lapdog of the Japanese?

69
00:06:02,236 --> 00:06:05,239
I just shot a Government-General official,

70
00:06:06,324 --> 00:06:08,034
and my little sister is dead.

71
00:06:08,993 --> 00:06:11,537
And yet here I am,
because I want to save you two.

72
00:06:11,621 --> 00:06:12,789
What more can I do

73
00:06:13,790 --> 00:06:15,375
to prove myself?

74
00:06:15,958 --> 00:06:17,251
Do you think I'd fall for that?

75
00:06:19,545 --> 00:06:21,714
Bring your father here.
He might still be alive.

76
00:06:24,175 --> 00:06:25,385
Let her go.

77
00:06:25,468 --> 00:06:27,887
I'll kill you in front of your father.

78
00:06:28,388 --> 00:06:29,222
You'll pay

79
00:06:30,306 --> 00:06:33,267
for what you did to my brother.

80
00:06:34,352 --> 00:06:35,812
What are you talking about?

81
00:06:36,396 --> 00:06:37,563
Did you forget already?

82
00:06:38,523 --> 00:06:39,857
You killed him

83
00:06:40,608 --> 00:06:43,111
right here in the Government-General
at the banquet!

84
00:07:00,461 --> 00:07:02,088
The cook…

85
00:07:04,132 --> 00:07:05,299
He was your brother?

86
00:07:05,883 --> 00:07:08,344
That's right. He was my brother.

87
00:07:15,685 --> 00:07:16,561
Police!

88
00:07:16,644 --> 00:07:18,229
Drop your weapons and surrender!

89
00:07:24,610 --> 00:07:26,696
I'm Sato Hideo
from the Foreign Affairs Division.

90
00:07:27,738 --> 00:07:29,782
I'm in here. Don't do anything yet!

91
00:07:29,866 --> 00:07:31,993
The inspector general's son?

92
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:34,537
Mr. Sato, are you okay?

93
00:07:36,789 --> 00:07:38,124
Yes, I'm fine.

94
00:07:38,207 --> 00:07:39,375
That's a relief.

95
00:07:39,459 --> 00:07:41,878
No one was hurt
at the inspector general's residence!

96
00:07:43,754 --> 00:07:44,589
No one

97
00:07:45,339 --> 00:07:46,340
was hurt?

98
00:07:52,346 --> 00:07:53,306
So…

99
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:58,227
Is my little sister safe too?

100
00:07:59,479 --> 00:08:00,855
Your little sister?

101
00:08:03,357 --> 00:08:05,902
Yes. She's safe, as far as we know.

102
00:08:16,871 --> 00:08:17,872
I see.

103
00:08:19,248 --> 00:08:20,583
Please wait a moment!

104
00:08:20,666 --> 00:08:21,501
Yes, sir!

105
00:08:28,466 --> 00:08:29,383
I did not

106
00:08:30,593 --> 00:08:31,594
kill your brother.

107
00:08:31,677 --> 00:08:32,637
Don't lie to me.

108
00:08:35,056 --> 00:08:36,015
We don't have time.

109
00:08:37,058 --> 00:08:39,685
Get Ms. Lee out first,
making it look like she's your hostage.

110
00:08:39,769 --> 00:08:41,646
Then take me hostage so you can get out.

111
00:08:42,188 --> 00:08:44,357
They can't shoot me.
I'm the inspector general's son.

112
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:45,274
No.

113
00:08:46,442 --> 00:08:47,568
I'll let her go.

114
00:08:48,736 --> 00:08:50,363
But I'm not leaving here.

115
00:08:51,322 --> 00:08:52,532
Bring your father to me.

116
00:08:53,699 --> 00:08:55,785
I'll make him watch me kill you.

117
00:08:55,868 --> 00:08:59,205
Then I'll kill him and myself

118
00:09:00,498 --> 00:09:01,415
with this bomb.

119
00:09:07,797 --> 00:09:08,965
That means you lose.

120
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:10,675
What?

121
00:09:10,758 --> 00:09:12,093
Once my father gets here,

122
00:09:13,177 --> 00:09:15,638
the police will storm into this room.

123
00:09:15,721 --> 00:09:16,639
Then you'll die.

124
00:09:18,099 --> 00:09:20,393
My father wouldn't care if I died.

125
00:09:21,185 --> 00:09:24,272
He'd use my death for Japanese propaganda
against the independence fighters.

126
00:09:24,355 --> 00:09:26,148
Did you forget I have a bomb?

127
00:09:26,232 --> 00:09:28,109
If you set that bomb off,

128
00:09:29,860 --> 00:09:32,613
only you will die,
and my father will be safe.

129
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:35,324
Your brother's death…

130
00:09:37,326 --> 00:09:38,160
will be in vain.

131
00:09:40,913 --> 00:09:43,833
But if you take me hostage,

132
00:09:44,375 --> 00:09:45,918
you can make it out alive.

133
00:09:46,002 --> 00:09:47,712
They would never shoot me.

134
00:09:47,795 --> 00:09:51,215
I never intended
to leave here alive in the first place!

135
00:09:56,137 --> 00:09:57,221
Still…

136
00:10:01,392 --> 00:10:04,437
<i>you have comrades</i>
<i>waiting for you out there.</i>

137
00:10:07,356 --> 00:10:10,192
<i>They must be desperately wishing</i>
<i>for you to come out alive.</i>

138
00:10:12,361 --> 00:10:13,863
Just as you desperately wished

139
00:10:15,072 --> 00:10:16,324
for your brother…

140
00:10:18,701 --> 00:10:20,453
to return safely.

141
00:10:27,168 --> 00:10:28,002
I…

142
00:10:29,629 --> 00:10:31,130
did not kill your brother.

143
00:10:33,299 --> 00:10:36,886
I have no intention of killing you,
and I don't want you to die.

144
00:10:36,969 --> 00:10:38,721
If you still want me dead,

145
00:10:39,388 --> 00:10:41,599
make it out alive today

146
00:10:42,266 --> 00:10:44,060
and wait for another chance to kill me.

147
00:10:49,523 --> 00:10:50,441
As long as you live…

148
00:10:53,527 --> 00:10:54,862
you'll get another chance.

149
00:10:58,616 --> 00:10:59,533
<i>Se-hwan.</i>

150
00:11:00,117 --> 00:11:03,537
If something happens to me tomorrow--

151
00:11:03,621 --> 00:11:04,664
Come on.

152
00:11:04,747 --> 00:11:07,166
Don't say that. That's bad luck.

153
00:11:08,834 --> 00:11:11,921
That's why I said <i>if.</i>

154
00:11:15,841 --> 00:11:16,676
Even so,

155
00:11:17,301 --> 00:11:21,097
you have to live to see
Joseon become independent.

156
00:11:25,434 --> 00:11:28,396
You can't die before you see
Joseon gain independence.

157
00:11:30,189 --> 00:11:33,317
Remember how I fought to save you
during the Great Kantō Disaster.

158
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:36,737
Stay alive.

159
00:11:38,072 --> 00:11:38,906
Se-hwan.

160
00:11:40,950 --> 00:11:42,076
As long as you live,

161
00:11:43,577 --> 00:11:44,912
you'll get another chance.

162
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:02,221
Interpreter Sato is in there?

163
00:12:02,304 --> 00:12:04,390
Yes, it seems he's being held hostage.

164
00:12:05,808 --> 00:12:06,809
Break down the door.

165
00:12:08,477 --> 00:12:11,647
Then Interpreter Sato could get hurt.

166
00:12:11,731 --> 00:12:14,442
I don't care!
Break down the door and arrest them all!

167
00:12:20,906 --> 00:12:22,366
Keum Seo-hee!

168
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:23,367
Mr. Sato!

169
00:12:28,247 --> 00:12:29,582
Back off, all of you!

170
00:12:30,416 --> 00:12:32,752
If any of you try anything,

171
00:12:33,377 --> 00:12:35,838
I'll kill the inspector general's son!

172
00:12:39,175 --> 00:12:41,510
What should we do, Chief?

173
00:12:43,429 --> 00:12:44,263
Back off!

174
00:12:48,309 --> 00:12:49,602
The woman goes first.

175
00:12:59,361 --> 00:13:00,571
She has nothing to do with it.

176
00:13:10,706 --> 00:13:12,500
She has nothing to do with it!

177
00:13:19,340 --> 00:13:20,174
<i>Lee Ga-kyung.</i>

178
00:13:22,843 --> 00:13:24,595
Can you trust me just this once?

179
00:13:27,139 --> 00:13:30,684
No matter what I do or say?

180
00:13:37,441 --> 00:13:38,317
Yes.

181
00:13:40,236 --> 00:13:41,070
I trust you.

182
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:48,744
<i>Don't die.</i>

183
00:13:49,870 --> 00:13:50,788
<i>Please.</i>

184
00:13:55,835 --> 00:13:57,711
Now walk. Nice and slow.

185
00:14:03,259 --> 00:14:05,302
Don't even think about pulling anything,

186
00:14:05,386 --> 00:14:06,679
or I'll shoot you.

187
00:14:08,305 --> 00:14:09,306
All right.

188
00:14:11,392 --> 00:14:13,352
Everyone, please move back.

189
00:14:16,230 --> 00:14:17,314
Back off, all of you!

190
00:14:28,033 --> 00:14:29,118
What's going on?

191
00:14:32,830 --> 00:14:34,248
Se-hwan.

192
00:14:38,711 --> 00:14:39,545
Stand back!

193
00:14:41,714 --> 00:14:42,715
Stand back!

194
00:14:48,679 --> 00:14:49,680
Stand back!

195
00:15:03,903 --> 00:15:06,322
Make sure Keum Seo-hee stays safe.

196
00:15:07,656 --> 00:15:08,574
No need to tell me.

197
00:15:09,825 --> 00:15:11,201
I was going to do that anyway.

198
00:15:12,077 --> 00:15:12,912
You must be

199
00:15:13,871 --> 00:15:15,039
in love with her.

200
00:15:17,041 --> 00:15:20,628
I took you for a clever Japanese lapdog,
but you've fallen for a spy.

201
00:15:22,046 --> 00:15:23,505
I wish your father knew about it.

202
00:15:30,137 --> 00:15:31,555
You'd better stay alive too.

203
00:15:32,598 --> 00:15:33,557
See you again soon.

204
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:36,018
All right.

205
00:16:54,805 --> 00:16:56,348
Get the inspector general to safety!

206
00:16:56,432 --> 00:16:57,266
Sir!

207
00:16:57,349 --> 00:16:58,600
It's dangerous. This way!

208
00:17:25,252 --> 00:17:26,086
Se-hwan.

209
00:17:27,296 --> 00:17:28,464
Go after them!

210
00:17:38,891 --> 00:17:40,059
Hold on tight.

211
00:17:53,655 --> 00:17:54,573
What the hell?

212
00:17:58,494 --> 00:17:59,620
Move the car!

213
00:17:59,703 --> 00:18:00,913
Get the car out of here!

214
00:18:00,996 --> 00:18:02,122
Turn the car around!

215
00:18:03,040 --> 00:18:04,166
Hey, you!

216
00:18:04,249 --> 00:18:05,375
What the hell are you doing?

217
00:18:05,459 --> 00:18:07,711
Sorry, that car came out of nowhere--

218
00:18:09,338 --> 00:18:10,172
I'm sorry.

219
00:18:15,677 --> 00:18:17,513
I've seen that guy somewhere before.

220
00:18:17,596 --> 00:18:18,555
I'm so sorry.

221
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:30,359
Mr. Sato, please move over there.

222
00:18:38,992 --> 00:18:40,160
He's still alive!

223
00:18:49,545 --> 00:18:50,379
Songjeon.

224
00:18:51,755 --> 00:18:52,840
Are you watching over me?

225
00:18:56,009 --> 00:18:57,052
Guess what?

226
00:18:58,262 --> 00:19:00,222
I got a job at Gyeongdo Noodle House.

227
00:19:42,890 --> 00:19:43,974
The Gugukdan?

228
00:19:47,311 --> 00:19:49,980
First the opening ceremony,

229
00:19:50,063 --> 00:19:51,690
and now they planted a spy

230
00:19:51,773 --> 00:19:54,735
as the pneumatic tube system's
on-site supervisor

231
00:19:55,569 --> 00:19:57,696
and sent a bomb to the residence?

232
00:19:58,447 --> 00:20:00,073
They've been making a mockery

233
00:20:00,157 --> 00:20:02,284
of the Government-General under our noses.

234
00:20:02,993 --> 00:20:05,662
What the hell
have you been doing all this time?

235
00:20:05,746 --> 00:20:06,955
Your Excellency.

236
00:20:07,039 --> 00:20:07,915
At that time, I--

237
00:20:07,998 --> 00:20:10,209
Is the Government-General's security

238
00:20:10,292 --> 00:20:13,045
no better than a shop door
in the marketplace?

239
00:20:14,504 --> 00:20:16,465
Please forgive me, Your Excellency!

240
00:20:17,049 --> 00:20:19,259
The League of Nations
Commission of Enquiry

241
00:20:19,343 --> 00:20:21,136
is coming soon.

242
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:24,306
Instead of showing them a peaceful Joseon,

243
00:20:24,389 --> 00:20:26,558
are you planning to show complete chaos,

244
00:20:26,642 --> 00:20:28,727
with bombs going off everywhere?

245
00:20:28,810 --> 00:20:29,645
Sato!

246
00:20:30,479 --> 00:20:35,234
You said you knew how to handle them
because you were born in Joseon.

247
00:20:35,317 --> 00:20:39,238
Look at you, letting those <i>Josenjings</i>
make a fool of you.

248
00:20:39,321 --> 00:20:41,240
Is this what you meant by handling them?

249
00:20:42,741 --> 00:20:44,493
I'm sorry, Your Excellency!

250
00:20:46,411 --> 00:20:49,206
I made all the preparations
to round them all up,

251
00:20:50,165 --> 00:20:52,334
but the officers on the ground
misjudged the situation.

252
00:20:52,417 --> 00:20:54,044
"Misjudged the situation"?

253
00:20:55,295 --> 00:20:57,422
You've let the Gugukdan
make a fool of you.

254
00:20:57,506 --> 00:21:00,425
You couldn't even get
the Gyodang-ri slums under control.

255
00:21:00,509 --> 00:21:03,220
Is there anything you can do right?

256
00:21:04,388 --> 00:21:06,265
You're not getting away with this.

257
00:21:06,932 --> 00:21:09,226
The Japanese government
is keeping an eye on this.

258
00:21:11,144 --> 00:21:12,562
Because of this mess,

259
00:21:12,646 --> 00:21:15,399
I'm being summoned to Tokyo.

260
00:21:15,482 --> 00:21:16,525
Your Excellency.

261
00:21:17,234 --> 00:21:18,777
Before you leave,

262
00:21:18,860 --> 00:21:20,445
I'll make sure we deliver

263
00:21:20,529 --> 00:21:23,532
concrete results
on both the Gugukdan and Gyodang-ri.

264
00:21:24,157 --> 00:21:25,075
Results?

265
00:21:27,035 --> 00:21:30,747
You've already shown me plenty of results.

266
00:21:32,040 --> 00:21:35,919
I'll decide what to do with you
when I get back.

267
00:21:36,003 --> 00:21:37,087
Until then,

268
00:21:38,046 --> 00:21:39,298
keep your heads down.

269
00:21:43,427 --> 00:21:45,387
Yes, Your Excellency.

270
00:21:46,888 --> 00:21:48,265
Yes, Your Excellency!

271
00:21:55,230 --> 00:21:58,317
After everything I went through
to get where I am,

272
00:21:59,026 --> 00:22:02,029
he thinks he can cast me aside
over those worthless fools?

273
00:22:02,571 --> 00:22:03,697
Like hell he will!

274
00:22:06,742 --> 00:22:07,617
Inspector General.

275
00:22:07,701 --> 00:22:11,079
I clearly ordered to arrest Keum Seo-hee
just as you instructed.

276
00:22:11,163 --> 00:22:13,832
But my incompetent subordinates
botched the operation.

277
00:22:14,499 --> 00:22:15,542
I assure you, though,

278
00:22:15,625 --> 00:22:18,003
I'll make sure Gyodang-ri is dealt with.

279
00:22:18,086 --> 00:22:19,129
I'll send the police now--

280
00:22:19,212 --> 00:22:21,089
"Send the police"?

281
00:22:22,549 --> 00:22:24,134
You imbecile!

282
00:22:28,555 --> 00:22:31,767
Do you want a shootout
before the Commission arrives in Joseon?

283
00:22:31,850 --> 00:22:34,519
I gave that troublesome land
to Kim Seung-eok for a reason.

284
00:22:34,603 --> 00:22:35,771
Do I have to spell it out?

285
00:22:37,105 --> 00:22:39,358
You get someone else
to do your dirty work.

286
00:22:39,441 --> 00:22:43,779
Imagine the fallout if things go wrong
and the foreign press catches wind of it.

287
00:22:43,862 --> 00:22:46,406
Did you learn nothing from Kyeam-ri?

288
00:23:02,547 --> 00:23:04,925
The one who told us
to shoot them in Kyeam-ri

289
00:23:06,093 --> 00:23:07,260
was you.

290
00:23:15,685 --> 00:23:17,896
So you were born in Shanghai?

291
00:23:17,979 --> 00:23:20,607
Give me your parents' names and address.

292
00:23:21,316 --> 00:23:23,485
My husband's been taken to the hospital.

293
00:23:23,568 --> 00:23:24,945
I'll answer when he gets here.

294
00:23:25,028 --> 00:23:27,114
Just answer the question.

295
00:23:27,197 --> 00:23:28,824
Are you really Chinese?

296
00:23:34,329 --> 00:23:35,247
Inspector General!

297
00:24:00,689 --> 00:24:07,112
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

298
00:24:20,375 --> 00:24:23,795
Inspector General, I believe
there's been some misunderstanding.

299
00:24:23,879 --> 00:24:25,338
- Why is Mrs. Yoo--
- Misunderstanding?

300
00:24:29,676 --> 00:24:30,719
Keum Seo-hee.

301
00:24:32,304 --> 00:24:33,138
Yes?

302
00:24:33,221 --> 00:24:36,183
Why did you give her
your dead daughter's name?

303
00:24:37,976 --> 00:24:40,187
Did you need
a replacement for your dead kid?

304
00:24:47,861 --> 00:24:49,070
You should resent her.

305
00:24:52,407 --> 00:24:54,951
It's her fault for giving you
the name Keum Seo-hee.

306
00:24:59,581 --> 00:25:00,415
Got nothing to say?

307
00:25:03,126 --> 00:25:05,879
Will you keep your mouth shut
like your husband did

308
00:25:07,547 --> 00:25:08,798
even if I shoot her dead?

309
00:25:15,180 --> 00:25:18,600
You just don't care if she dies
because she's not your real daughter?

310
00:25:22,270 --> 00:25:24,564
Well, let's find out.

311
00:25:25,649 --> 00:25:26,650
Wait!

312
00:25:32,989 --> 00:25:35,909
If what you just said was true…

313
00:25:40,121 --> 00:25:42,207
then shooting me dead right here

314
00:25:43,333 --> 00:25:45,043
would be pointless, wouldn't it?

315
00:25:48,338 --> 00:25:50,257
They wouldn't speak
even when their own child died.

316
00:25:50,840 --> 00:25:53,468
Why would they care about me dying

317
00:25:54,177 --> 00:25:55,595
just because I share her name?

318
00:25:57,055 --> 00:25:58,056
You're quite the talker.

319
00:26:00,725 --> 00:26:01,643
Mrs. Yoo

320
00:26:02,352 --> 00:26:03,812
doesn't speak Japanese very well.

321
00:26:08,567 --> 00:26:12,112
I'm not sure
what happened between you two.

322
00:26:12,946 --> 00:26:13,989
But, Inspector General,

323
00:26:14,698 --> 00:26:17,200
if you want to know about them,

324
00:26:17,742 --> 00:26:19,494
wouldn't it be better

325
00:26:20,579 --> 00:26:21,413
to use me

326
00:26:22,414 --> 00:26:24,791
than to kill me?

327
00:26:38,096 --> 00:26:40,807
Joseon women really do have
a reckless streak.

328
00:26:41,975 --> 00:26:43,560
It can get them killed

329
00:26:44,060 --> 00:26:44,978
or keep them alive.

330
00:26:54,446 --> 00:26:55,405
Keum Seok-jung

331
00:26:56,781 --> 00:26:58,241
died in that very spot.

332
00:27:05,457 --> 00:27:07,042
No, sir! You can't go in!

333
00:27:07,125 --> 00:27:07,959
You can't!

334
00:27:08,668 --> 00:27:09,628
Get out of my way!

335
00:27:18,386 --> 00:27:19,346
Honey.

336
00:27:21,890 --> 00:27:23,558
Sir, can you explain this?

337
00:27:23,642 --> 00:27:24,893
Why'd you arrest my wife?

338
00:27:25,602 --> 00:27:28,521
She knew a bomb would arrive
through the pneumatic tube.

339
00:27:28,605 --> 00:27:31,483
Don't you recall the bombing
at the pneumatic tube opening ceremony?

340
00:27:33,026 --> 00:27:36,029
Every paper received disturbing tips
blaming the independence fighters,

341
00:27:36,112 --> 00:27:37,697
so I warned her to stay alert.

342
00:27:37,781 --> 00:27:40,033
That's why my wife thought
it might be a bomb

343
00:27:40,116 --> 00:27:41,993
and rushed to save your daughter.

344
00:27:42,077 --> 00:27:43,828
How is that a crime?

345
00:27:45,580 --> 00:27:46,623
Well, Inspector General?

346
00:27:46,706 --> 00:27:49,417
Have I ever put the Government-General
in a difficult position?

347
00:27:50,877 --> 00:27:54,422
Regardless of what other
foreign journalists say about Joseon,

348
00:27:54,506 --> 00:27:57,425
I've always been fair
and truthful in my coverage.

349
00:27:57,509 --> 00:27:59,302
Even after the bombing at the banquet,

350
00:27:59,386 --> 00:28:02,430
I was the only one who reported
the Government-General's position!

351
00:28:08,978 --> 00:28:10,772
Out of respect for you,

352
00:28:10,855 --> 00:28:14,859
I even asked the head of our Far East
branch who's coming to Gyeongseong

353
00:28:14,943 --> 00:28:18,655
with the League of Nations Commission,
to meet you privately for tea.

354
00:28:18,738 --> 00:28:21,157
After all that,
how can you treat me like this?

355
00:28:22,992 --> 00:28:24,452
My wife is American too.

356
00:28:26,287 --> 00:28:29,332
Does Japan usually lock up foreigners
without any evidence?

357
00:28:29,416 --> 00:28:30,792
Then you'll have to arrest me too.

358
00:28:33,837 --> 00:28:35,296
My wife rushed to the study

359
00:28:35,380 --> 00:28:37,632
because I'd told her
to watch out for a bomb.

360
00:28:46,975 --> 00:28:49,018
You're a journalist through and through.

361
00:28:49,811 --> 00:28:52,814
That was very logical and convincing,
almost as if you'd rehearsed it.

362
00:28:55,817 --> 00:28:57,026
Just as you told me.

363
00:29:02,657 --> 00:29:03,867
Escort them home.

364
00:29:04,576 --> 00:29:05,410
Yes, sir!

365
00:29:08,580 --> 00:29:10,498
Guard their home until further notice.

366
00:29:10,582 --> 00:29:13,042
Don't let a single soul get in or out.

367
00:29:13,126 --> 00:29:15,003
Yes, sir!

368
00:29:15,086 --> 00:29:16,254
Just as you said,

369
00:29:16,921 --> 00:29:18,423
given how disturbing things are.

370
00:29:21,009 --> 00:29:22,010
Shall we go, honey?

371
00:29:28,308 --> 00:29:30,143
Keum Seo-hee, you're staying here.

372
00:29:35,732 --> 00:29:37,358
We should finish our conversation.

373
00:29:49,078 --> 00:29:51,623
What did you want to talk about?

374
00:29:54,125 --> 00:29:56,085
Are you planning to use me?

375
00:29:59,088 --> 00:30:00,006
Or…

376
00:30:02,425 --> 00:30:04,052
are you going to kill me?

377
00:30:04,135 --> 00:30:05,053
Neither.

378
00:30:06,930 --> 00:30:08,139
It won't be me who kills you.

379
00:30:08,973 --> 00:30:10,433
It'll be them.

380
00:30:13,019 --> 00:30:15,730
Now that you've been alone with me,

381
00:30:17,607 --> 00:30:19,359
they will never trust you again.

382
00:30:21,820 --> 00:30:23,071
Go ask them…

383
00:30:25,532 --> 00:30:27,700
about my dead Joseon wife.

384
00:30:29,744 --> 00:30:30,578
She was a spy

385
00:30:31,955 --> 00:30:34,415
the Gugukdan sent to me.

386
00:30:38,253 --> 00:30:39,254
What did you say?

387
00:30:43,591 --> 00:30:45,260
So they did keep it from you.

388
00:30:46,845 --> 00:30:49,514
They sent someone
as young as you to work as a spy.

389
00:30:50,557 --> 00:30:52,392
They really are ruthless.

390
00:30:56,104 --> 00:30:57,146
A spy?

391
00:31:01,150 --> 00:31:02,026
You mean me?

392
00:31:03,236 --> 00:31:04,946
No, I'm not a spy.

393
00:31:05,613 --> 00:31:08,741
You know that.
I used to be their live-in maid.

394
00:31:08,825 --> 00:31:11,619
Now I'm an English interpreter trainee
at the Government-General.

395
00:31:11,703 --> 00:31:12,620
If you say so.

396
00:31:14,831 --> 00:31:16,624
They did make sure you looked the part.

397
00:31:19,377 --> 00:31:21,004
No matter how loyal you are,

398
00:31:22,046 --> 00:31:24,591
the Gugukdan will kill you
once you're no longer useful.

399
00:31:26,843 --> 00:31:28,177
That's how she died too.

400
00:31:30,471 --> 00:31:31,764
<i>It belongs to my mother.</i>

401
00:31:31,848 --> 00:31:33,683
I'm looking for my mother,

402
00:31:34,726 --> 00:31:36,603
but I don't even know her name yet.

403
00:31:38,187 --> 00:31:41,149
You may tell Hideo the truth,
if that's what you want.

404
00:31:41,232 --> 00:31:43,860
It seems like you and my son
have become quite close.

405
00:31:45,111 --> 00:31:46,321
I'll let you decide.

406
00:31:57,999 --> 00:31:59,792
You stink.

407
00:32:02,003 --> 00:32:03,087
It's the smell of someone

408
00:32:03,171 --> 00:32:07,175
who crawled their way
out of the muck just to survive.

409
00:32:12,639 --> 00:32:14,724
You're just like me.

410
00:32:36,579 --> 00:32:37,705
You have the same eyes.

411
00:32:43,920 --> 00:32:46,339
Do you think killing me
will bring Joseon's independence?

412
00:32:47,340 --> 00:32:48,174
No.

413
00:32:48,967 --> 00:32:50,385
It will never happen.

414
00:32:51,886 --> 00:32:53,388
And yet those Gugukdan bastards

415
00:32:53,471 --> 00:32:56,182
keep manipulating innocent people
and dragging them to their graves,

416
00:32:56,265 --> 00:32:57,475
just as they've done to you.

417
00:32:59,102 --> 00:33:01,104
Even if you die here and now,

418
00:33:01,187 --> 00:33:03,106
they won't lift a finger to keep you alive

419
00:33:03,731 --> 00:33:06,359
or even try to save you.

420
00:33:08,319 --> 00:33:09,988
So many people have died already,

421
00:33:10,071 --> 00:33:12,949
but they won't stop this lunacy.
Don't you get it?

422
00:33:23,292 --> 00:33:24,127
You have five days.

423
00:33:26,546 --> 00:33:29,841
Bring me proof that Yoo Philip
and his wife are with the Gugukdan.

424
00:33:31,509 --> 00:33:32,468
Proof that his wife

425
00:33:33,344 --> 00:33:35,388
was Keum Seok-jung's wife
will also suffice.

426
00:33:37,890 --> 00:33:39,767
Do that, and I'll spare your life.

427
00:33:39,851 --> 00:33:42,103
But if you can't…

428
00:33:45,606 --> 00:33:47,150
it'd be a shame to waste your talent,

429
00:33:47,233 --> 00:33:48,735
but I'll kill you first.

430
00:33:50,528 --> 00:33:52,030
Just like Keum Seok-jung,

431
00:33:52,613 --> 00:33:53,781
who died right here.

432
00:33:56,576 --> 00:33:58,244
Don't even think about running.

433
00:34:01,748 --> 00:34:02,790
Because…

434
00:34:07,545 --> 00:34:10,339
I can track you down
and kill you at any time.

435
00:36:14,672 --> 00:36:16,716
I don't care if you're a spy or not.

436
00:36:18,885 --> 00:36:20,303
Just promise me.

437
00:36:23,723 --> 00:36:25,516
Promise me you won't die.

438
00:36:31,230 --> 00:36:32,064
Please.

439
00:36:35,276 --> 00:36:36,986
Please, just stay alive,

440
00:36:37,904 --> 00:36:38,738
Ga-kyung.

441
00:36:41,824 --> 00:36:43,451
<i>You promise me too.</i>

442
00:36:45,369 --> 00:36:46,329
<i>Promise</i>

443
00:36:47,205 --> 00:36:48,664
<i>you won't die.</i>

444
00:37:58,651 --> 00:37:59,735
What are you doing?

445
00:37:59,819 --> 00:38:03,030
Sato will want hard evidence
linking us to the Gugukdan.

446
00:38:03,114 --> 00:38:05,199
I'm sure he told her to bring that proof.

447
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:09,745
Philip, Seo-hee gave up going to America
and came back for us.

448
00:38:09,829 --> 00:38:11,455
Unlike before, I trust her too.

449
00:38:11,539 --> 00:38:13,249
But we're dealing with Ishikawa.

450
00:38:13,332 --> 00:38:16,502
Ishikawa was known for his ruthless
and devious interrogations

451
00:38:16,585 --> 00:38:18,796
at Jongno Police Station.

452
00:38:19,880 --> 00:38:21,757
So we have to take precautions.

453
00:38:22,466 --> 00:38:24,343
And this doesn't just put us at risk.

454
00:38:24,427 --> 00:38:26,804
It could put
the entire Gugukdan in danger.

455
00:38:26,887 --> 00:38:29,056
She knows so much about us, after all.

456
00:38:36,939 --> 00:38:37,773
So-ran.

457
00:38:40,318 --> 00:38:41,235
Don't forget.

458
00:38:42,820 --> 00:38:45,573
She's not your daughter, Seo-hee.
She's Lee Ga-kyung, the pickpocket.

459
00:38:45,656 --> 00:38:46,490
That girl

460
00:38:48,284 --> 00:38:50,328
is only Seo-hee
because you called her that.

461
00:38:56,208 --> 00:39:00,212
Does she have anything that could prove
we're members of the Gugukdan?

462
00:39:02,840 --> 00:39:03,674
Yes.

463
00:39:05,092 --> 00:39:07,178
The identity guarantee letter
for her trip to America

464
00:39:08,054 --> 00:39:10,264
and the Government-General
staff booklet Suzuki made.

465
00:39:10,348 --> 00:39:11,223
I have one condition.

466
00:39:12,058 --> 00:39:13,267
I need you to promise me

467
00:39:14,560 --> 00:39:17,480
that when Seo-hee comes back,
you'll hear her out first

468
00:39:18,689 --> 00:39:20,149
instead of doubting or accusing her.

469
00:40:10,783 --> 00:40:12,368
I found the identity guarantee letter.

470
00:40:15,162 --> 00:40:16,163
I found the booklet.

471
00:40:21,293 --> 00:40:22,711
What do you think you're doing?

472
00:40:25,840 --> 00:40:26,924
I asked what you're doing.

473
00:40:37,351 --> 00:40:38,185
What's this for?

474
00:40:41,063 --> 00:40:42,773
Did you go through my things

475
00:40:44,066 --> 00:40:45,484
to take these back?

476
00:40:46,527 --> 00:40:47,361
Why?

477
00:40:48,070 --> 00:40:49,113
Calm down.

478
00:40:49,196 --> 00:40:50,948
I'll explain everything,
so just calm down.

479
00:40:51,532 --> 00:40:52,658
You want me to calm down?

480
00:40:53,576 --> 00:40:54,743
I just

481
00:40:55,619 --> 00:40:58,038
risked my life to carry out the operation.

482
00:40:58,122 --> 00:40:59,039
After all that,

483
00:41:00,666 --> 00:41:02,334
this is what you're doing to me?

484
00:41:03,461 --> 00:41:05,754
We just needed to make sure.

485
00:41:05,838 --> 00:41:07,381
Make sure of what?

486
00:41:07,965 --> 00:41:09,341
What did you and Sato talk about?

487
00:41:14,054 --> 00:41:14,889
What?

488
00:41:18,642 --> 00:41:21,687
You think I might have tipped him off.

489
00:41:21,770 --> 00:41:23,606
That's why you're doing this?

490
00:41:24,231 --> 00:41:27,526
Do you think
I'll bring these pieces of paper to Sato?

491
00:41:27,610 --> 00:41:28,903
I want an answer.

492
00:41:30,237 --> 00:41:31,947
How did you escape the Government-General,

493
00:41:32,031 --> 00:41:34,116
and what did you and Sato
discuss at Jongno Station?

494
00:41:34,742 --> 00:41:35,618
Mr. Yoo.

495
00:41:35,701 --> 00:41:36,535
Seo-hee.

496
00:41:37,745 --> 00:41:39,413
Just tell us what happened.

497
00:41:39,497 --> 00:41:41,207
If nothing happened, just say so--

498
00:41:41,290 --> 00:41:43,459
Is it that hard for you to trust me?

499
00:41:46,003 --> 00:41:47,171
Do you…

500
00:41:49,256 --> 00:41:51,592
Do you have any idea
how terrified I was today?

501
00:41:54,678 --> 00:41:57,056
Even if he was an awful Japanese man,

502
00:41:57,139 --> 00:41:59,934
I saw someone die right in front of me.

503
00:42:00,851 --> 00:42:02,645
And that <i>naengmyeon </i>deliveryman…

504
00:42:06,857 --> 00:42:08,859
Your comrade Se-hwan.

505
00:42:09,902 --> 00:42:12,571
I did my best to find a way
to make it out alive with him.

506
00:42:12,655 --> 00:42:13,572
But…

507
00:42:18,994 --> 00:42:19,828
I made it out

508
00:42:21,080 --> 00:42:22,331
by making it look like

509
00:42:22,414 --> 00:42:24,917
he'd been holding me hostage.

510
00:42:25,626 --> 00:42:28,629
Interpreter Sato offered himself
as a hostage to get him out,

511
00:42:28,712 --> 00:42:30,005
but it didn't work out.

512
00:42:30,089 --> 00:42:32,841
After that, I was taken
to Jongno Police Station.

513
00:42:32,925 --> 00:42:34,468
That's all there is to it.

514
00:42:37,263 --> 00:42:41,600
Interpreter Kim Tae-ung
shot that Japanese man to save us.

515
00:42:44,603 --> 00:42:45,437
Wait.

516
00:42:47,356 --> 00:42:48,315
Kim Tae-ung?

517
00:42:52,152 --> 00:42:53,612
You mean Sato Hideo?

518
00:42:55,364 --> 00:42:56,198
Yes.

519
00:42:58,617 --> 00:43:00,202
That's his Joseon name.

520
00:43:04,123 --> 00:43:08,460
I told you never to develop feelings
for Sato Hideo, didn't I?

521
00:43:09,587 --> 00:43:12,840
That's how you stay alive as a spy.

522
00:43:18,846 --> 00:43:19,763
Well, actually…

523
00:43:24,643 --> 00:43:25,561
you said

524
00:43:27,062 --> 00:43:29,315
he shot the cook
on the day of the banquet.

525
00:43:32,484 --> 00:43:34,320
Are you sure you saw it yourself?

526
00:43:36,488 --> 00:43:38,073
Could you have been mistaken?

527
00:43:40,534 --> 00:43:43,162
You're hoping So-ran was mistaken,
aren't you?

528
00:43:59,553 --> 00:44:01,347
Thank you so much

529
00:44:02,014 --> 00:44:03,057
for saving me.

530
00:44:07,269 --> 00:44:08,479
The one who saved you

531
00:44:09,980 --> 00:44:11,357
was my wife.

532
00:44:12,650 --> 00:44:14,818
Thank you, ma'am.

533
00:44:15,819 --> 00:44:17,279
Are you all right?

534
00:44:17,363 --> 00:44:18,405
Yes.

535
00:44:18,489 --> 00:44:20,282
Are you all right too, ma'am?

536
00:44:22,242 --> 00:44:24,787
I've been hoping to meet you someday.

537
00:44:26,413 --> 00:44:27,623
Sorry?

538
00:44:27,706 --> 00:44:30,000
We already met earlier.

539
00:44:34,171 --> 00:44:35,506
Hanako, it's time to go.

540
00:44:35,589 --> 00:44:37,424
We should let them get some rest.

541
00:44:37,966 --> 00:44:38,801
Okay.

542
00:44:47,518 --> 00:44:48,560
Here.

543
00:44:58,362 --> 00:44:59,279
Well then.

544
00:44:59,363 --> 00:45:01,365
Bye, Hanako.

545
00:45:02,324 --> 00:45:03,158
Wait.

546
00:45:03,242 --> 00:45:06,995
You sound like the woman on the phone
who said she was Hideo's girlfriend.

547
00:45:07,913 --> 00:45:08,747
Hanako.

548
00:45:08,831 --> 00:45:12,042
Ms. Yanagi's been waiting outside.
Let's get going.

549
00:45:12,126 --> 00:45:13,001
Yeah.

550
00:45:13,085 --> 00:45:14,294
It was her voice.

551
00:45:15,087 --> 00:45:16,130
Am I wrong?

552
00:45:21,301 --> 00:45:24,012
I'm sorry I didn't listen to you earlier.

553
00:45:26,265 --> 00:45:28,058
I'm glad you weren't hurt.

554
00:45:28,142 --> 00:45:31,019
See? It was the same voice.

555
00:45:34,148 --> 00:45:35,983
We'll be going then.

556
00:45:36,650 --> 00:45:38,235
Once again, I'm deeply grateful

557
00:45:39,695 --> 00:45:41,071
for saving Hanako.

558
00:45:43,031 --> 00:45:44,742
Take care, Mr. Hideo.

559
00:45:53,584 --> 00:45:54,418
Bye.

560
00:46:16,940 --> 00:46:19,735
I don't think you can do
any more work as a spy.

561
00:46:20,986 --> 00:46:22,070
I'll find somewhere safe.

562
00:46:22,154 --> 00:46:24,031
Quit the Government-General and lie low.

563
00:46:26,533 --> 00:46:27,826
<i>No matter how loyal you are,</i>

564
00:46:28,452 --> 00:46:30,746
the Gugukdan will kill you
once you're no longer useful.

565
00:46:32,539 --> 00:46:34,500
No, I'll go to work.

566
00:46:36,251 --> 00:46:37,085
What?

567
00:46:38,212 --> 00:46:39,713
If I disappear now,

568
00:46:39,797 --> 00:46:41,673
it'll look like I'm a spy.

569
00:46:41,757 --> 00:46:43,467
- Don't you think?
- But…

570
00:46:45,344 --> 00:46:46,178
Good night.

571
00:47:18,168 --> 00:47:19,002
What?

572
00:47:21,588 --> 00:47:22,756
The inspector general

573
00:47:22,840 --> 00:47:25,634
ordered you to arrest Sato Hideo?

574
00:47:25,717 --> 00:47:26,635
Yes.

575
00:47:26,718 --> 00:47:29,429
So we were waiting
at Myeongwolgwan for further orders.

576
00:47:29,513 --> 00:47:30,597
Myeongwolgwan?

577
00:47:32,140 --> 00:47:35,811
Kim Seung-eok's daughter
was supposed to meet him at Hwawol.

578
00:47:35,894 --> 00:47:39,231
We were told Mr. Sato
would come to Myeongwolgwan alone.

579
00:47:41,066 --> 00:47:42,985
- Okay. That'll be all.
- Yes, sir.

580
00:47:47,155 --> 00:47:51,994
It seems he and his beloved son
aren't getting along anymore.

581
00:47:52,077 --> 00:47:56,123
He can't even keep
his own <i>Josenjing </i>son under control,

582
00:47:57,708 --> 00:48:00,961
yet he dared to lecture me about Kyeam-ri?

583
00:48:12,931 --> 00:48:14,266
I'm sorry, miss.

584
00:48:18,103 --> 00:48:21,565
I drove straight at their car
without asking you.

585
00:48:21,648 --> 00:48:24,902
Now that they've found the gun,
it may not be easy to get out.

586
00:48:27,446 --> 00:48:28,280
But

587
00:48:28,947 --> 00:48:30,741
they'll let you go for sure.

588
00:48:33,076 --> 00:48:35,203
I can tough it out here,

589
00:48:35,829 --> 00:48:36,747
so don't worry.

590
00:48:39,708 --> 00:48:42,753
I'll tell my dad that going
to the Government-General was my idea.

591
00:48:56,767 --> 00:48:57,809
My apologies.

592
00:49:04,066 --> 00:49:05,651
There's been a misunderstanding.

593
00:49:14,952 --> 00:49:16,787
Tail those two,
and don't let them catch on.

594
00:49:16,870 --> 00:49:17,704
Yes, sir.

595
00:49:21,166 --> 00:49:22,417
<i>He went that way.</i>

596
00:49:22,501 --> 00:49:23,794
He ran out that way.

597
00:49:23,877 --> 00:49:26,713
It's a tall, young guy with a mask on.

598
00:49:28,340 --> 00:49:29,925
Close the curtains!

599
00:49:30,008 --> 00:49:32,970
She's the daughter of the president
of Joil Textile Factory.

600
00:49:35,305 --> 00:49:38,433
His son is suspicious enough,
and now the daughter-in-law too?

601
00:49:41,478 --> 00:49:43,981
After being played by that spy bitch,

602
00:49:44,064 --> 00:49:45,816
he still hasn't learned his lesson.

603
00:49:48,443 --> 00:49:51,363
And he's got the nerve
to throw me under the bus?

604
00:49:57,494 --> 00:50:00,080
As Interpreter Sato testified,
the pneumatic tube room supervisor

605
00:50:00,163 --> 00:50:03,625
used a <i>naengmyeon </i>delivery as an excuse
to let the Gugukdan into the building.

606
00:50:04,126 --> 00:50:06,378
The guard at the side entrance
also confirmed it.

607
00:50:08,130 --> 00:50:10,716
The follow-up investigation
into Interpreter Sato resumes--

608
00:50:10,799 --> 00:50:12,092
"Follow-up investigation"?

609
00:50:13,468 --> 00:50:14,469
Yes, sir.

610
00:50:14,553 --> 00:50:16,680
My son killed the spy

611
00:50:16,763 --> 00:50:19,141
and nearly lost his own life as a hostage.

612
00:50:20,225 --> 00:50:22,102
What more is there to investigate?

613
00:50:22,936 --> 00:50:24,104
The thing is--

614
00:50:24,187 --> 00:50:25,313
Are you saying

615
00:50:25,397 --> 00:50:27,357
you suspect my own son?

616
00:50:28,775 --> 00:50:30,444
Absolutely not, sir!

617
00:50:30,527 --> 00:50:32,446
- You're dismissed.
- Yes, sir!

618
00:50:46,585 --> 00:50:49,171
You can sleep here, just for tonight.

619
00:50:49,963 --> 00:50:51,131
Okay.

620
00:50:51,214 --> 00:50:53,091
By the way,

621
00:50:54,342 --> 00:50:57,429
what do you call "big sister"
in the Joseon language?

622
00:50:57,512 --> 00:50:59,097
What? Big sister?

623
00:51:02,142 --> 00:51:03,101
<i>Unni.</i>

624
00:51:04,478 --> 00:51:05,729
<i>"Unni"?</i>

625
00:51:07,481 --> 00:51:08,440
<i>Unni.</i>

626
00:51:09,524 --> 00:51:11,401
You know what?

627
00:51:11,485 --> 00:51:12,694
Yanagi…

628
00:51:12,778 --> 00:51:14,404
I mean, Ms. Yanagi said

629
00:51:14,488 --> 00:51:18,617
you were going to marry a Joseon woman.

630
00:51:18,700 --> 00:51:20,327
Is that <i>"unni" </i>the one?

631
00:51:22,287 --> 00:51:23,663
I approve!

632
00:51:23,747 --> 00:51:25,999
I like that <i>"unni."</i>

633
00:51:28,001 --> 00:51:30,295
I can't believe
what that little mouth says.

634
00:51:31,546 --> 00:51:32,506
Now go to sleep.

635
00:52:01,243 --> 00:52:02,077
How's Hanako?

636
00:52:02,953 --> 00:52:03,870
She's asleep.

637
00:52:04,621 --> 00:52:05,455
All right.

638
00:52:06,832 --> 00:52:08,875
She must've been shaken.

639
00:52:08,959 --> 00:52:09,793
Yes.

640
00:52:12,129 --> 00:52:13,839
Father will probably lose his position.

641
00:52:15,382 --> 00:52:17,008
After what happened at the banquet,

642
00:52:17,676 --> 00:52:19,177
today's incident makes it inevitable.

643
00:52:20,720 --> 00:52:22,013
If he's forced out,

644
00:52:22,973 --> 00:52:24,891
he'll probably never make it back
into politics.

645
00:52:28,854 --> 00:52:30,438
It's for the best for everyone.

646
00:52:32,274 --> 00:52:33,942
It should've happened long ago.

647
00:52:35,569 --> 00:52:38,280
What are you going to do?

648
00:52:39,948 --> 00:52:41,074
Are you going

649
00:52:42,242 --> 00:52:43,410
with your father?

650
00:52:44,494 --> 00:52:45,370
To Japan?

651
00:52:50,584 --> 00:52:52,335
The inspector general is home.

652
00:53:57,817 --> 00:53:59,778
I've told the police everything.

653
00:53:59,861 --> 00:54:01,571
I have nothing more to say.

654
00:54:02,572 --> 00:54:03,615
Hope you get some rest.

655
00:54:04,532 --> 00:54:06,493
Surely you have something to say to me.

656
00:54:16,294 --> 00:54:18,088
Being taken hostage was a mistake.

657
00:54:19,297 --> 00:54:20,131
I'm sorry.

658
00:54:22,425 --> 00:54:24,511
Still, you saved my life, Father.

659
00:54:24,594 --> 00:54:28,515
Did you want to save that <i>Josenjing?</i>

660
00:54:32,519 --> 00:54:35,397
When you faced that cook
who attacked me at the opening ceremony,

661
00:54:36,064 --> 00:54:37,232
you hesitated.

662
00:54:39,109 --> 00:54:41,820
If I'd left him to you
instead of shooting him myself,

663
00:54:42,362 --> 00:54:44,614
would you have let yourself
be taken hostage then?

664
00:54:46,741 --> 00:54:47,909
To save him?

665
00:54:56,167 --> 00:54:57,168
Hideo.

666
00:54:57,877 --> 00:55:00,130
What's making you so confused?

667
00:55:08,722 --> 00:55:10,181
The police told me something.

668
00:55:12,684 --> 00:55:14,185
That it wasn't Kim Seung-eok

669
00:55:14,769 --> 00:55:16,896
waiting for me today, but his daughter.

670
00:55:18,565 --> 00:55:20,442
She was at Hwawol, not Myeongwolgwan.

671
00:55:22,736 --> 00:55:25,071
Why did you tell me
to go to Myeongwolgwan?

672
00:55:26,656 --> 00:55:28,658
Who was waiting for me there?

673
00:55:30,368 --> 00:55:31,202
Confused?

674
00:55:32,370 --> 00:55:33,913
Aren't you the one who's confused?

675
00:55:33,997 --> 00:55:35,206
Shut your mouth, Hideo.

676
00:55:35,290 --> 00:55:38,251
It's true I wanted to know
what drove those in the Gugukdan.

677
00:55:38,335 --> 00:55:39,711
You want to know why?

678
00:55:39,794 --> 00:55:41,129
Independence for Korea!

679
00:55:41,212 --> 00:55:42,047
Hideo!

680
00:55:42,130 --> 00:55:43,757
Because they keep risking their lives,

681
00:55:43,840 --> 00:55:47,093
shouting "Independence for Korea"
even when they know they'll die.

682
00:55:47,594 --> 00:55:49,137
That's why I wanted to know

683
00:55:49,804 --> 00:55:51,931
what could possibly drive them to do it.

684
00:55:53,767 --> 00:55:57,520
I wanted to know
what it was about Joseon's independence

685
00:55:59,022 --> 00:56:01,608
that made them risk their lives
without the slightest fear.

686
00:56:02,984 --> 00:56:04,069
But then…

687
00:56:08,948 --> 00:56:09,949
today,

688
00:56:10,909 --> 00:56:12,577
they tried to kill Hanako.

689
00:56:14,746 --> 00:56:16,414
My one and only sister.

690
00:56:20,627 --> 00:56:22,962
I can never forgive them, Father.

691
00:56:26,216 --> 00:56:27,592
Instead of doubting me,

692
00:56:29,010 --> 00:56:30,095
keep me by your side.

693
00:56:33,390 --> 00:56:35,183
I will not betray you.

694
00:56:37,936 --> 00:56:39,145
At least, not anymore.

695
00:57:13,555 --> 00:57:16,808
Simply because I'm a colonial resident,
born and raised in Joseon,

696
00:57:17,475 --> 00:57:20,437
I've spent my whole life
having to prove myself.

697
00:57:21,729 --> 00:57:23,314
This time will be no different.

698
00:57:23,815 --> 00:57:25,525
I'll prove myself again.

699
00:57:26,151 --> 00:57:28,528
After all I've been through
to get this far,

700
00:57:29,612 --> 00:57:31,573
I can't go down like this.

701
00:57:34,951 --> 00:57:36,244
Have they made you step down?

702
00:57:39,622 --> 00:57:41,583
I want you to interpret
the farewell speech

703
00:57:41,666 --> 00:57:45,336
at Gyeongseong Station on the day
the League of Nations Commission leaves.

704
00:57:45,962 --> 00:57:48,173
The Government-General's top priority now

705
00:57:48,256 --> 00:57:50,049
is the success of the Commission's visit.

706
00:57:50,717 --> 00:57:52,177
We must prove

707
00:57:52,886 --> 00:57:55,680
that Japan's rule over Joseon
is legitimate.

708
00:57:57,599 --> 00:57:58,516
That said…

709
00:58:00,602 --> 00:58:04,772
though you're Joseon by blood,
you're loyal to the Empire of Japan.

710
00:58:06,024 --> 00:58:08,943
What better symbol
of peace and harmony in Joseon…

711
00:58:11,070 --> 00:58:12,906
could there be than you?

712
00:58:14,240 --> 00:58:15,325
Would that…

713
00:58:17,619 --> 00:58:18,703
help you too?

714
00:58:18,786 --> 00:58:19,787
Help?

715
00:58:22,123 --> 00:58:22,957
Yes.

716
00:58:24,876 --> 00:58:26,169
It most certainly would.

717
00:58:29,756 --> 00:58:32,217
Do you think I'll give up so easily?

718
00:58:34,886 --> 00:58:35,720
No.

719
00:58:37,430 --> 00:58:39,516
I will never back down.

720
00:58:41,643 --> 00:58:42,519
Not ever.

721
00:58:47,565 --> 00:58:49,984
SIN TAE-JIN

722
00:59:13,925 --> 00:59:15,134
You need to leave Gyeongseong.

723
00:59:24,894 --> 00:59:26,062
My father already knows

724
00:59:26,771 --> 00:59:29,440
who Yoo Philip, his wife,
and you really are.

725
00:59:33,361 --> 00:59:35,446
I don't mean to disregard your wishes.

726
00:59:38,700 --> 00:59:39,534
But…

727
00:59:39,617 --> 00:59:40,577
No.

728
00:59:44,122 --> 00:59:47,125
It's more dangerous to run at this point.

729
00:59:49,502 --> 00:59:53,339
They say it's safest
right under the tiger's nose.

730
01:00:11,983 --> 01:00:13,901
Here, take this.

731
01:00:20,033 --> 01:00:21,659
Remember what I told you before?

732
01:00:23,911 --> 01:00:26,080
This pawn ticket belonged to my mother.

733
01:00:29,459 --> 01:00:31,336
Right after she gave birth to Hanako,

734
01:00:32,503 --> 01:00:33,504
she left us.

735
01:00:35,673 --> 01:00:38,176
That's why people assumed
she'd died giving birth.

736
01:00:41,846 --> 01:00:42,805
But my father

737
01:00:44,057 --> 01:00:46,768
never said otherwise.

738
01:00:50,021 --> 01:00:51,481
I suppose he was too hurt

739
01:00:52,565 --> 01:00:54,233
by the fact that she'd left him.

740
01:01:00,490 --> 01:01:01,574
I would find myself…

741
01:01:05,161 --> 01:01:06,371
thinking of my mother…

742
01:01:08,456 --> 01:01:10,041
every so often.

743
01:01:12,460 --> 01:01:14,253
Maybe I missed her.

744
01:01:16,839 --> 01:01:17,674
No.

745
01:01:19,509 --> 01:01:21,886
I do miss her.

746
01:01:26,391 --> 01:01:28,309
I don't know why she had a pawn ticket

747
01:01:28,393 --> 01:01:30,603
that belonged to someone
named Sin Tae-jin.

748
01:01:32,855 --> 01:01:34,649
But if I find that Jongno Pawnshop

749
01:01:36,067 --> 01:01:38,361
and retrieve the item…

750
01:01:40,780 --> 01:01:43,449
maybe it'll lead me to her.

751
01:01:47,161 --> 01:01:48,579
Mr. Sato.

752
01:01:53,751 --> 01:01:56,379
Though I haven't had any luck yet.

753
01:02:00,133 --> 01:02:01,175
On the day of the banquet,

754
01:02:01,926 --> 01:02:03,219
you returned this to me.

755
01:02:04,303 --> 01:02:05,596
You were leaving, weren't you?

756
01:02:08,766 --> 01:02:10,017
You don't need to answer.

757
01:02:11,310 --> 01:02:12,520
But this time…

758
01:02:15,064 --> 01:02:17,275
you said you wouldn't leave.

759
01:02:22,947 --> 01:02:24,490
So please, keep this with you.

760
01:02:27,869 --> 01:02:29,287
That way, I can feel…

761
01:02:35,376 --> 01:02:37,545
you're safe by my side.

762
01:02:41,591 --> 01:02:42,467
You are…

763
01:02:45,887 --> 01:02:46,888
my vault.

764
01:02:49,974 --> 01:02:51,934
Hold on to it, and next time…

765
01:02:54,395 --> 01:02:55,563
we'll find…

766
01:02:58,357 --> 01:03:00,568
Jongno Pawnshop together.

767
01:04:05,049 --> 01:04:06,717
<i>No matter how loyal you are,</i>

768
01:04:06,801 --> 01:04:09,554
<i>the Gugukdan will kill you</i>
<i>once you're no longer useful.</i>

769
01:04:09,637 --> 01:04:11,097
<i>That's how she died too.</i>

770
01:04:16,602 --> 01:04:18,229
<i>Can I keep</i>

771
01:04:19,689 --> 01:04:22,191
<i>trusting you, madam?</i>

772
01:04:30,825 --> 01:04:31,909
<i>Can I keep</i>

773
01:04:33,661 --> 01:04:35,454
<i>trusting you?</i>

774
01:05:09,947 --> 01:05:11,949
Once I walk out of this house,

775
01:05:12,033 --> 01:05:13,826
I might never be able to come back.

776
01:05:16,203 --> 01:05:18,372
Because the Gugukdan could get rid of me.

777
01:05:18,956 --> 01:05:22,168
Once you leave,
the police might storm into the house.

778
01:05:25,630 --> 01:05:27,632
Because you could turn us in.

779
01:06:03,042 --> 01:06:04,043
Good morning.

780
01:06:04,627 --> 01:06:06,295
Interpreter Trainee Keum Seo-hee.

781
01:06:12,134 --> 01:06:12,969
Yes?

782
01:06:13,636 --> 01:06:15,179
INTERPRETER TRAINEE KEUM SEO-HEE

783
01:06:17,848 --> 01:06:20,226
Why are my things here?

784
01:06:24,397 --> 01:06:25,314
Good morning, sir.

785
01:06:28,985 --> 01:06:29,860
You're here?

786
01:06:30,945 --> 01:06:32,947
Yamada suddenly decided to quit.

787
01:06:34,740 --> 01:06:35,950
Welcome.

788
01:06:36,993 --> 01:06:38,744
You're my secretary starting today.

789
01:06:43,124 --> 01:06:44,458
Four days left now.

790
01:06:58,472 --> 01:06:59,473
Mr. Suzuki?

791
01:07:01,892 --> 01:07:02,810
Good to see you again.

792
01:07:03,728 --> 01:07:05,855
I was called back to work rather suddenly.

793
01:07:05,938 --> 01:07:07,440
INTERPRETER SUZUKI HIROYUKI

794
01:07:24,790 --> 01:07:25,624
Good morning.

795
01:07:26,250 --> 01:07:27,084
Secretary?

796
01:07:27,710 --> 01:07:28,586
Mr. Sato.

797
01:07:29,420 --> 01:07:30,421
What in the world…

798
01:07:31,005 --> 01:07:34,216
Gyodang-ri is hardly
the issue right now, isn't it?

799
01:07:35,342 --> 01:07:37,053
I want to call off the engagement.

800
01:07:37,136 --> 01:07:39,096
Had I known you'd lose your position,

801
01:07:39,180 --> 01:07:41,932
I'd never have signed
a marriage contract to begin with.

802
01:07:42,016 --> 01:07:44,143
- "Marriage contract."
- If His Excellency finds out--

803
01:07:44,226 --> 01:07:45,186
Mr. Kim.

804
01:07:54,236 --> 01:07:55,404
Keep your voice down.

805
01:07:56,322 --> 01:07:58,616
Are you trying to tell
the whole city about our deal?

806
01:08:00,034 --> 01:08:01,452
I mean, first the banquet bombing,

807
01:08:02,119 --> 01:08:04,288
then even your residence yesterday…

808
01:08:04,371 --> 01:08:07,166
The independence fighters
have made a complete fool of you.

809
01:08:07,249 --> 01:08:10,878
The Government-General is in shambles.
How could you escape the fallout?

810
01:08:10,961 --> 01:08:12,713
So now you want to back out?

811
01:08:12,797 --> 01:08:13,714
Of course.

812
01:08:13,798 --> 01:08:16,092
What kind of businessman
would agree to lose money?

813
01:08:16,175 --> 01:08:19,595
Since things have gone south,
we should settle up and part ways.

814
01:08:20,721 --> 01:08:22,264
Let's call off the engagement.

815
01:08:23,808 --> 01:08:24,767
Call it off, is it?

816
01:08:25,559 --> 01:08:26,393
Very well.

817
01:08:27,478 --> 01:08:28,854
Then let's settle up first,

818
01:08:28,938 --> 01:08:30,689
just as you suggested.

819
01:08:32,066 --> 01:08:33,984
Do you have the money for the penalty?

820
01:08:34,610 --> 01:08:35,528
Inspector General.

821
01:08:35,611 --> 01:08:38,114
You had no complaints
when you got that land cheap.

822
01:08:39,073 --> 01:08:41,826
You were busy counting
all the money you'd make off me.

823
01:08:41,909 --> 01:08:43,744
Now you want to ignore the contract?

824
01:08:43,828 --> 01:08:44,662
What?

825
01:08:45,704 --> 01:08:48,624
Let's get our facts straight.

826
01:08:49,458 --> 01:08:51,877
You think I bought that dump
because I wanted to?

827
01:08:51,961 --> 01:08:55,297
I only agreed to take on the headache
of developing that land

828
01:08:55,381 --> 01:08:58,926
because you promised
to back me as inspector general.

829
01:08:59,009 --> 01:09:02,596
But now you're about to lose
that position, aren't you?

830
01:09:07,101 --> 01:09:08,477
Who said I'd lose my position?

831
01:09:13,566 --> 01:09:14,525
You have four days.

832
01:09:15,943 --> 01:09:19,155
Clear that miserable Gyodang-ri slum
once and for all within four days.

833
01:09:19,238 --> 01:09:21,031
I mean,

834
01:09:21,115 --> 01:09:25,035
you said we had until the Commission
arrived to demolish the shantytown.

835
01:09:25,119 --> 01:09:25,953
No.

836
01:09:27,454 --> 01:09:28,330
Four days.

837
01:09:29,456 --> 01:09:30,749
Clear it out completely.

838
01:09:30,833 --> 01:09:33,002
But four days is pushing it.

839
01:09:33,627 --> 01:09:35,754
Those residents are refusing to move.

840
01:09:36,380 --> 01:09:38,674
What if someone ends up dead
in the process?

841
01:09:41,719 --> 01:09:43,637
Don't test my patience any further.

842
01:09:44,805 --> 01:09:45,890
Mr. Kim.

843
01:09:59,069 --> 01:10:01,697
So this is a petition
to stop the demolition,

844
01:10:01,780 --> 01:10:03,282
and you just need our thumbprints?

845
01:10:03,365 --> 01:10:06,660
That's right. I had it drawn up
at a scrivener's office in Jongno.

846
01:10:06,744 --> 01:10:10,748
If Joil Textile, the Government-General,
the Keijo Municipal Office, and the press

847
01:10:10,831 --> 01:10:12,416
all see this, they'll have to listen.

848
01:10:13,209 --> 01:10:15,211
It's all pointless.

849
01:10:16,003 --> 01:10:18,797
If that had worked, would we have had
to leave home and end up here?

850
01:10:19,673 --> 01:10:22,551
These pieces of paper
will end up as toilet paper.

851
01:10:23,469 --> 01:10:26,138
It's better than doing nothing
and getting kicked out.

852
01:10:26,222 --> 01:10:27,264
Listen, kid.

853
01:10:27,348 --> 01:10:29,808
I screamed for independence
until my throat gave out.

854
01:10:29,892 --> 01:10:32,937
But all I've got is this crippled leg.

855
01:10:33,646 --> 01:10:35,147
They'll kick us out, so don't bother.

856
01:10:35,231 --> 01:10:36,774
Hey, Bak-chun.

857
01:10:36,857 --> 01:10:40,611
Don't you think
it's worth giving this petition a shot?

858
01:10:40,694 --> 01:10:41,904
Good grief.

859
01:10:41,987 --> 01:10:43,781
With the money to write the petition,

860
01:10:43,864 --> 01:10:46,242
we might as well
buy Kkot-nim a bowl of noodles.

861
01:10:46,325 --> 01:10:47,409
Noodles?

862
01:10:49,703 --> 01:10:50,537
I'm signing.

863
01:10:53,332 --> 01:10:54,500
THE PEOPLE OF GYODANG-RI

864
01:10:56,252 --> 01:10:57,086
Geum-ok.

865
01:10:57,169 --> 01:10:58,921
Why are we always being forced out?

866
01:10:59,421 --> 01:11:00,589
We've lost our country.

867
01:11:00,673 --> 01:11:02,800
If we're thrown out of here,
where else can we go?

868
01:11:03,801 --> 01:11:05,886
Are we supposed to take their beatings,
obey them,

869
01:11:05,970 --> 01:11:07,721
and leave whenever they tell us to?

870
01:11:07,805 --> 01:11:09,598
No, we're human beings too.

871
01:11:16,355 --> 01:11:18,274
I'll leave on my terms,
even if it kills me.

872
01:11:19,149 --> 01:11:20,567
I'm standing my ground here.

873
01:11:22,027 --> 01:11:23,279
I'm tired of being thrown out.

874
01:11:25,781 --> 01:11:27,074
My goodness.

875
01:11:27,574 --> 01:11:29,535
I'm sick of being kicked out too.
Give it here.

876
01:11:30,577 --> 01:11:33,497
It's just a thumbprint.
I can do it a hundred times over.

877
01:11:33,580 --> 01:11:34,623
Here.

878
01:11:35,749 --> 01:11:37,084
Pass it here.

879
01:11:37,167 --> 01:11:38,877
- Me too.
- Let me do it too.

880
01:11:42,840 --> 01:11:43,966
By the way, No-ma.

881
01:11:44,049 --> 01:11:45,968
Isn't Ga-kyung going
to give her fingerprint?

882
01:11:46,051 --> 01:11:47,136
When is she coming back?

883
01:11:48,846 --> 01:11:49,763
Ga-kyung?

884
01:11:52,099 --> 01:11:53,684
I don't think she'll come back.

885
01:11:54,268 --> 01:11:55,436
She won't? Why?

886
01:11:59,148 --> 01:12:00,691
Why would you hit me?

887
01:12:00,774 --> 01:12:02,901
How could you say
such awful things to her?

888
01:12:04,361 --> 01:12:05,195
<i>So it's true.</i>

889
01:12:05,279 --> 01:12:08,032
First you serve the Japs like a dog,
and now you're messing around with one?

890
01:12:08,115 --> 01:12:09,283
Just like your mom?

891
01:12:12,202 --> 01:12:14,580
A child doesn't get
to choose their parents.

892
01:12:14,663 --> 01:12:17,666
That poor thing.
Imagine how much she must've struggled

893
01:12:18,709 --> 01:12:20,627
because of her mother,
who didn't even raise her.

894
01:12:20,711 --> 01:12:22,004
- No-ma.
- It's my fault.

895
01:12:22,087 --> 01:12:24,214
Collect all the petitions for me.

896
01:12:24,298 --> 01:12:25,632
Kkot-nim, I'll be back.

897
01:12:25,716 --> 01:12:26,800
Want another beating?

898
01:12:26,884 --> 01:12:28,635
Bye, No-ma!

899
01:12:34,558 --> 01:12:35,934
You jerks.

900
01:12:37,061 --> 01:12:41,899
I was just getting lucky,
and you had to ruin my game, damn it.

901
01:12:48,697 --> 01:12:49,823
My hand!

902
01:12:49,907 --> 01:12:51,492
Get your foot off my hand!

903
01:12:51,575 --> 01:12:54,453
Do you think we're just suckers
who burn money on you?

904
01:12:55,037 --> 01:12:58,582
We paid you 50 won to get rid
of those filthy shantytown bums.

905
01:12:58,665 --> 01:13:01,335
You should have something to show for it.

906
01:13:04,880 --> 01:13:06,256
Come on, sir.

907
01:13:06,799 --> 01:13:08,634
Fifty won sounds like a lot,

908
01:13:08,717 --> 01:13:11,428
but each household only gets a won or two.

909
01:13:11,929 --> 01:13:15,057
Where are they supposed to go with that?

910
01:13:15,140 --> 01:13:16,141
So,

911
01:13:16,683 --> 01:13:19,144
you blew all that money gambling?

912
01:13:20,020 --> 01:13:22,189
I've done enough.

913
01:13:22,856 --> 01:13:25,109
Then give me another 30 won or so.

914
01:13:26,276 --> 01:13:27,569
Those bums

915
01:13:27,653 --> 01:13:31,407
need a cart to haul their stuff out.

916
01:13:37,496 --> 01:13:39,873
Damn it, you bastards!

917
01:13:49,633 --> 01:13:51,260
Do you think this is a game?

918
01:13:52,177 --> 01:13:53,053
Listen carefully.

919
01:13:55,139 --> 01:13:56,140
Easy with the knife.

920
01:13:56,890 --> 01:13:58,058
You have three days.

921
01:13:58,142 --> 01:13:59,726
Throw them all out by then,

922
01:13:59,810 --> 01:14:01,770
or you'll pay
for that 50 won with your life.

923
01:14:01,854 --> 01:14:03,522
How can I do that in three days?

924
01:14:03,605 --> 01:14:05,023
If you can't,

925
01:14:05,107 --> 01:14:07,651
cough up all the money you pocketed.

926
01:14:08,861 --> 01:14:09,695
Is that clear?

927
01:14:09,778 --> 01:14:10,612
Yes, sir.

928
01:14:11,530 --> 01:14:12,781
Crystal clear.

929
01:14:19,663 --> 01:14:20,497
Let's go.

930
01:14:24,334 --> 01:14:25,919
Those rotten thugs.

931
01:14:27,212 --> 01:14:28,714
I almost got myself killed.

932
01:14:30,757 --> 01:14:33,469
How am I supposed to get those bums out?

933
01:14:43,520 --> 01:14:44,354
Right.

934
01:14:45,355 --> 01:14:48,192
Hello, this is
the Inspector General's Office.

935
01:14:51,236 --> 01:14:54,114
You must've enjoyed
making a fool of me yesterday.

936
01:14:54,823 --> 01:14:57,493
I can't leave my desk for too long.

937
01:14:57,576 --> 01:14:59,203
Please get to the point.

938
01:15:00,996 --> 01:15:02,080
Lee Ga-kyung.

939
01:15:08,337 --> 01:15:10,255
My name is Keum Seo-hee.

940
01:15:10,923 --> 01:15:13,258
I think you've mistaken me
for someone else.

941
01:15:13,342 --> 01:15:15,135
In May 1929,

942
01:15:15,886 --> 01:15:17,221
Mount Yebong, Gyeonggi-do.

943
01:15:21,850 --> 01:15:24,394
Shimomura, who lived
in Hwanggeumjeong 2-jeongmok,

944
01:15:24,478 --> 01:15:27,731
reportedly got drunk and fell to his death
in a valley on Mount Yebong.

945
01:15:28,357 --> 01:15:30,692
The geisha who was there with him,

946
01:15:31,902 --> 01:15:33,529
Sakura, disappeared.

947
01:15:36,198 --> 01:15:38,992
<i>She left nothing</i>
<i>but a bloodstained stone on the cliff.</i>

948
01:15:42,329 --> 01:15:45,999
The restaurant owner
recognized your photo right away.

949
01:15:49,795 --> 01:15:52,297
Apparently, the 100 won you owed
when you were sold

950
01:15:52,798 --> 01:15:55,467
has now grown to 350 won with interest.

951
01:15:56,051 --> 01:15:56,885
Right.

952
01:15:57,678 --> 01:15:58,720
Don't worry.

953
01:16:00,556 --> 01:16:03,475
I didn't tell them you are here.

954
01:16:04,309 --> 01:16:05,143
What is it…

955
01:16:08,605 --> 01:16:09,898
you want to tell me?

956
01:16:11,358 --> 01:16:15,529
Find out who the inspector general meets,
what he's up to, and what he's hiding.

957
01:16:16,154 --> 01:16:17,781
Dig up any dirt on him,

958
01:16:17,864 --> 01:16:21,326
anything I can use against him,
and report back.

959
01:16:21,410 --> 01:16:22,244
Understood?

960
01:16:23,704 --> 01:16:26,248
How am I supposed to find all that out?

961
01:16:26,999 --> 01:16:28,709
I'm just his secretary.

962
01:16:33,046 --> 01:16:34,131
"Just"?

963
01:16:34,214 --> 01:16:37,050
You're a spy from the Gugukdan,
now you're his secretary.

964
01:16:37,134 --> 01:16:38,218
And you call that "just"?

965
01:16:39,261 --> 01:16:42,472
The inspector general
could have had you ripped to pieces,

966
01:16:43,599 --> 01:16:46,351
yet instead of arresting you,
he made you his secretary.

967
01:16:50,147 --> 01:16:51,231
Why would he do that?

968
01:16:53,317 --> 01:16:55,944
I just can't make sense of this.

969
01:16:57,154 --> 01:17:00,282
I just transferred to where they sent me.

970
01:17:02,117 --> 01:17:02,951
Whatever.

971
01:17:04,411 --> 01:17:09,374
Whether you're with the Gugukdan or not,
I couldn't care less right now.

972
01:17:14,004 --> 01:17:16,131
Find dirt on the inspector general.

973
01:17:17,174 --> 01:17:18,675
And whatever you see or hear,

974
01:17:18,759 --> 01:17:21,386
you report to me first,
before the inspector general.

975
01:17:22,512 --> 01:17:23,513
If you don't,

976
01:17:24,348 --> 01:17:28,018
you'll be executed for the murder
of the mainland Japanese resident.

977
01:17:30,479 --> 01:17:34,441
A <i>Josenjing </i>wench killed a Japanese man
and dumped his body?

978
01:17:36,902 --> 01:17:39,738
Imagine how thrilled
the Jongno police would be.

979
01:17:43,784 --> 01:17:46,286
Think wisely.

980
01:17:49,331 --> 01:17:50,499
Lee Ga-kyung.

981
01:18:35,961 --> 01:18:37,504
Let me ask you one thing.

982
01:18:37,587 --> 01:18:39,047
Hanako's mom…

983
01:18:41,133 --> 01:18:42,551
Did the Gugukdan kill her?

984
01:18:44,845 --> 01:18:46,012
What do you mean?

985
01:18:46,096 --> 01:18:48,223
That's what the inspector general told me.

986
01:18:49,015 --> 01:18:52,310
She was a spy for the Gugukdan,
and when she was no longer useful,

987
01:18:54,187 --> 01:18:55,564
they killed her.

988
01:18:59,985 --> 01:19:00,819
Yes.

989
01:19:01,737 --> 01:19:02,571
That's right.

990
01:19:07,117 --> 01:19:09,244
We were just as responsible for her death.

991
01:19:09,953 --> 01:19:12,164
We tried to save her, but we failed.

992
01:19:14,458 --> 01:19:16,585
Even if I were in the same situation
as yesterday,

993
01:19:16,668 --> 01:19:17,878
I'd still save Hanako.

994
01:19:17,961 --> 01:19:18,795
Because to me,

995
01:19:20,422 --> 01:19:22,007
she's not Sato's daughter.

996
01:19:23,550 --> 01:19:26,344
She's the daughter of a woman
I sent undercover.

997
01:19:41,526 --> 01:19:43,653
<i>She had another daughter.</i>

998
01:19:45,197 --> 01:19:47,199
The girl she had before marrying Sato.

999
01:19:49,493 --> 01:19:51,077
Because of me, that little girl

1000
01:19:51,661 --> 01:19:53,872
was torn away
from her mother at a young age

1001
01:19:55,165 --> 01:19:56,708
and ended up dying all alone.

1002
01:20:00,629 --> 01:20:02,214
I'd already let that girl die.

1003
01:20:03,757 --> 01:20:07,093
I couldn't bear to lose Hanako too.

1004
01:20:10,138 --> 01:20:12,516
I don't even know
the name of her dead daughter.

1005
01:20:13,600 --> 01:20:16,394
I've carried the guilt
over that child for all these years.

1006
01:20:21,274 --> 01:20:22,108
Seo-hee.

1007
01:20:23,652 --> 01:20:24,569
Ga-kyung.

1008
01:20:26,530 --> 01:20:28,156
If anything happens to you…

1009
01:20:31,284 --> 01:20:33,537
I'll carry that pain
for the rest of my life.

1010
01:20:47,634 --> 01:20:48,510
I have decided…

1011
01:20:53,390 --> 01:20:55,183
to trust you.

1012
01:20:57,894 --> 01:21:01,439
It doesn't matter if you can't trust me.

1013
01:21:01,523 --> 01:21:03,191
I'm putting my trust in you.

1014
01:21:04,901 --> 01:21:05,819
We have no choice…

1015
01:21:08,113 --> 01:21:11,324
but to trust each other.

1016
01:21:25,922 --> 01:21:26,756
I trust you

1017
01:21:28,383 --> 01:21:29,634
as well.

1018
01:21:56,745 --> 01:21:57,996
Madam.

1019
01:22:01,708 --> 01:22:04,127
I think there's a way…

1020
01:22:15,472 --> 01:22:16,681
to get rid of Sato.

1021
01:22:19,559 --> 01:22:20,393
What?

1022
01:22:21,269 --> 01:22:23,605
You want to do what with me?

1023
01:22:26,900 --> 01:22:28,193
Let's make a deal.

1024
01:23:14,906 --> 01:23:18,827
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

1025
01:23:18,910 --> 01:23:22,414
<i>Sato, Fukuda, and Kim Seung-eok.</i>

1026
01:23:22,497 --> 01:23:25,166
I think these three will go
for each other's throats.

1027
01:23:25,250 --> 01:23:27,168
It's like getting bitten
by the dog I raised.

1028
01:23:27,252 --> 01:23:29,004
<i>Can you handle it on your own?</i>

1029
01:23:29,087 --> 01:23:30,755
<i>If you bring nothing in three days,</i>

1030
01:23:30,839 --> 01:23:32,507
you'll be in trouble yourself.

1031
01:23:32,590 --> 01:23:34,843
<i>Did you have a good day out today?</i>

1032
01:23:34,926 --> 01:23:36,302
<i>Yes, I had a good time.</i>

1033
01:23:36,386 --> 01:23:37,804
<i>You should be more worried</i>

1034
01:23:37,887 --> 01:23:40,390
about coming back empty-handed
than getting caught.

1035
01:23:40,473 --> 01:23:42,559
It has to be
the Inspector General's Office cabinet.

1036
01:23:42,642 --> 01:23:44,185
<i>You're still on the Gugukdan's side.</i>

1037
01:23:44,269 --> 01:23:45,854
<i>He's back at the Government-General.</i>

1038
01:23:47,355 --> 01:23:48,857
<i>You think I don't know that?</i>

1039
01:23:54,446 --> 01:23:56,448
Subtitle translation by: Youji Kim
